      "marks": 3,
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Explanation: For a valid PDF: f(x) ≥ 0 for all x, and ∫f(x)dx = 1. On [-1,0): 1/b > 0 requires b > 0. On [0,1]: ax(x+1)\n(x-1) = ax(x²-1). For 0 ≤ x ≤ 1, x ≥ 0 and (x²-1) ≤ 0, so we need a < 0. Integration: 1/b × 1 + ∫₀¹ ax(x²-1)dx = 1. ∫₀¹\nx(x²-1)dx = [x⁴/4 - x²/2]₀¹ = 1/4 - 1/2 = -1/4. So 1/b + a(-1/4) = 1, i.e., 1/b - a/4 = 1. With a=-3: 1/b + 3/4 = 1, so\n1/b = 1/4, b=4. Check: a=-3, b=4."
        }
      ],
